=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: pc1
diagnosis_text:
pc1's eth0 interface has been misconfigured with a /30 prefix length
(1.0.0.5/30) instead of the correct /8 that the rest of the server
segment uses. Router2's eth0, which is the LAN-side gateway, is
configured as 1.0.0.1/8, placing it in the 1.0.0.0/8 network. With
a /30 mask, pc1 treats its directly connected subnet as 1.0.0.4/30
(hosts 1.0.0.5–1.0.0.6, broadcast 1.0.0.7). The gateway address
1.0.0.1 falls in the 1.0.0.0/30 block — a completely different /30
segment — so the Linux kernel refuses to ARP for it and returns
"Network is unreachable" immediately. Compounding this, there is no
default route at all in pc1's routing table; only the kernel-generated
connected route 1.0.0.4/30 is present. The interface itself (eth0) is
up and link-layer reachability to switch4/router2 is fine — the fault
is purely in the IP addressing layer on pc1 alone.

Root cause: pc1's eth0 was reconfigured during the maintenance task
with an incorrect /30 subnet mask instead of /8, making the gateway
unreachable at the IP level and leaving no default route.

Corrective fix: Reconfigure pc1's eth0 address to 1.0.0.5/8 and add
a default route via 1.0.0.1. In practice: run
  ip addr replace 1.0.0.5/8 dev eth0
  ip route add default via 1.0.0.1
and persist the correct mask (/8) and gateway in the startup
configuration so it survives a reboot.
=== END ===
